  "measurement_note": "Size is n, the legal number of squares. Tiers 8, 64, and 256 span 32x. Square i has side 2(i+1) and vertical center n, so the complete union is vertically symmetric and the exact answer is n. Distinct bottom, top, left, and right edges keep many intervals active while exercising coordinate compression and segment-tree updates. The accepted sweep is O(n log n); a correct sweep that sorts and merges all active intervals anew at every event is O(n^2 log n) and must finish all outputs but fail scaling.",
